# Ropes.Blit: "world" (5 characters of S from index 6) copied into DST at
# index 2, and the rest of DST left as it was.  The Ada Ropes port's
# equivalent is rope_tool's copyslice (Ropes.Copy_Slice).
program RopeTool
arg blit
arg hello world
arg 6
arg XXXXXXXXX
arg 2
arg 5
status 0
output
XXworldXX
